# E §5 step 1 (tally 2.3, #247; C-4's clause; the critic's n1_q.tally): with t a hole, κ₀ is that hole: a later version
# that changes the instance (a1, known 2026-03-20, replaces amt) makes an adjustment whose existence is the hole, and so
# is a binding over `adjustments` that could hold it (adj). Pinned, the day decides: 03-05 and 03-12 give one adjustment,
# 03-20 none (the version is known on the day). Before: adj was 0 where two pinned days give 1 (#244 n1).
=== m.tally
model bk20260320
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input d_at: date
move pay: transfers
  on w
  at d_at
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  w = ?"which day is the pay?" "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"
ask adj: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask adj_p: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-20
ask adj_p05: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-05
ask adj_p12: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-12
=== expect
adj: ?"which day is the pay?" (w)
  cut 2026-06-10
adj_p: 0
  cut 2026-06-10
adj_p05: 1
  pinned: w = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-06-10
adj_p12: 1
  pinned: w = 2026-03-12
  cut 2026-06-10
